        <div class="statml-takeaways"><span class="content-kicker">The causal chain</span><ul><li><strong>You choose</strong> the architecture, activations, optimizer, and learning rate.</li><li><strong>Data</strong> enters and a forward pass produces predictions.</li><li><strong>Loss</strong> converts prediction error into an objective.</li><li><strong>Backpropagation computes gradients only.</strong></li><li><strong>The optimizer updates every weight and bias.</strong></li><li><strong>Updated parameters</strong> change the next forward pass.</li><li><strong>Validation</strong> identifies the checkpoint that generalizes best.</li><li><strong>Testing, deployment, monitoring, and error analysis</strong> keep the model accountable after training.</li></ul></div>
        <div class="formula-block">data → forward pass → loss → backprop gradients
→ optimizer step → updated weights → repeat</div>
